@essay rh="HOUSE AUREM · HANNAH · THE MACHINERY AROUND HER"
# The machinery around her
drop: Hannah works inside the Trials as staff, which means the machinery runs through her hands every day. She knows where it's blind, the back staircases and the camera gaps (TL), and she's built her life on acting only where she can.
The rules around her daughter are fixed. Eligibility isn't entry, anyone can submit a name, and Naomi can submit her own (FR 27). A child's status comes through household registration, so Naomi is eligible through Hannah's household and standing, whatever her father's place (FR 31–32). The only door out of the Trials' reach is a lower designation (FR 29).
Underneath all of it is 2085, the cohort that was assembled and measured and then sent home when Crest died and the Trial was cancelled (FR 34, FR 39). INFERENCE: Hannah was one of the twelve. She's never said it out loud, and Naomi doesn't know (FR 30).
side:
chips: TL, FR 27–34
k: The exit
stext: A designation lower than the Trials reach. It saves Naomi from the ladder by taking her off it.
marg
see: Vol. I, the designations, {v1:designations}.
/end

@page rh="HOUSE AUREM · HANNAH · EXCAVATION · 2085" m="TKC: FR 34 · FR 39; INFERENCE; WRITING"
# The Trial that didn't happen
INFERENCE: In 2085 Hannah was one of twelve young women assembled, prepared and measured against each other, and then Crest died mid-cycle, Dorian's accession forced a transition, and the Trial was cancelled. The twelve went home with their designations intact and no placements (FR 34, FR 39).
